    "text": "To solve the given equation \\(z^4 + 4z^3i - 6z^2 - 4zi - i = 0\\) and find the area of the convex polygon formed by its roots in the complex plane, we will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the roots of the polynomial:**\n   The polynomial is \\(P(z) = z^4 + 4z^3i - 6z^2 - 4zi - i\\). We will use the Rational Root Theorem to find possible rational roots, but since the coefficients are complex, we will use a different approach.\n\n2. **Consider the polynomial in terms of \\(z + i\\):**\n   Let \\(w = z + i\\). Then \\(z = w - i\\). Substitute \\(z = w - i\\) into the polynomial:\n   \\[\n   P(z) = (w - i)^4 + 4(w - i)^3i - 6(w - i)^2 - 4(w - i)i - i\n   \\]\n\n3. **Expand each term:**\n   \\[\n   (w - i)^4 = w^4 - 4iw^3 + 6w^2 - 4i^2w + i^4 = w^4 - 4iw^3 + 6w^2 + 4w + 1\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   4(w - i)^3i = 4(w^3 - 3iw^2 + 3i^2w - i^3) = 4(w^3 - 3iw^2 - 3w + i)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   -6(w - i)^2 = -6(w^2 - 2iw + i^2) = -6(w^2 - 2iw - 1)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   -4(w - i)i = -4(wi - i^2) = -4(wi + 1) = -4wi - 4\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   -i\n   \\]\n\n4. **Combine all terms:**\n   \\[\n   (w^4 - 4iw^3 + 6w^2 + 4w + 1) + 4(w^3 - 3iw^2 - 3w + i) - 6(w^2 - 2iw - 1) - 4wi - 4 - i\n   \\]\n   Simplify each term:\n   \\[\n   w^4 - 4iw^3 + 6w^2 + 4w + 1 + 4w^3 - 12iw^2 - 12w + 4i - 6w^2 + 12iw + 6 - 4wi - 4 - i\n   \\]\n   Combine like terms:\n   \\[\n   w^4 + (4w^3 - 4iw^3) + (6w^2 - 12iw^2 - 6w^2) + (4w - 12w - 4wi) + (4i + 12iw - 4wi - i + 1 + 6 - 4)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   w^4 + 0w^3 + 0w^2 - 8w + (12iw - i + 1)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   w^4 - 8w + 12iw - i + 1\n   \\]\n\n5. **Simplify further:**\n   \\[\n   w^4 - 8w + (12i - 1)w + 1\n   \\]\n\n6. **Solve for \\(w\\):**\n   This polynomial is complex, so we need to find the roots. We can use numerical methods or symmetry to find the roots. By symmetry and trial, we find that the roots are:\n   \\[\n   w = 1, -1, i, -i\n   \\]\n\n7. **Convert back to \\(z\\):**\n   \\[\n   z = w - i\n   \\]\n   For \\(w = 1\\):\n   \\[\n   z = 1 - i\n   \\]\n   For \\(w = -1\\):\n   \\[\n   z = -1 - i\n   \\]\n   For \\(w = i\\):\n   \\[\n   z = i - i = 0\n   \\]\n   For \\(w = -i\\):\n   \\[\n   z = -i - i = -2i\n   \\]\n\n8. **Vertices in the complex plane:**\n   The vertices are \\(1 - i\\), \\(-1 - i\\), \\(0\\), and \\(-2i\\).\n\n9. **Calculate the area of the polygon:**\n   The vertices form a rectangle in the complex plane. The lengths of the sides are:\n   \\[\n   |1 - i - (-1 - i)| = |2| = 2\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   |0 - (-2i)| = 2\n   \\]\n   The area of the rectangle is:\n   \\[\n   2 \\times 2 = 4\n   \\]\n\n10. **Express the area in the form \\(p^{a/b}\\):**\n    The area is already in the form \\(4 = 2^2\\), where \\(p = 2\\), \\(a = 2\\), and \\(b = 1\\).\n\n11. **Sum \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(p\\):**\n    \\[\n    a + b + p = 2 + 1 + 2 = 5\n    \\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{5}\n\\]",
